{number: 105}
{title: Who Is On the Lord’s Side?}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] Who is on the Lord's side? Who will serve the King?
[C] Who will be His [G] helpers, other [D7] lives to bring?
[G] Who will leave the world's side? Who will face the foe?
[C] Who is on the [G] Lord's side? Who for [D7] Him will [G] go?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G] By Thy call of mercy, by Thy grace divine,
We are [C] on the [G] Lord's side—Savior, [D7] we are [G] Thine!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G] Not for weight of glory, nor for crown and palm,
[C] Enter we the [G] army, raise the [D7] warrior psalm;
[G] But for Love that claimeth lives for whom He died:
[C] He whom Jesus [G] loveth halts on [D7] neither [G] side.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] Jesus, Thou hast bought us, not with gold or gem,
[C] But with Thine own [G] lifeblood, for Thy [D7] diadem;
[G] With Thy blessing filling each who comes to Thee,
[C] Thou hast made us [G] willing, Thou hast [D7] made us [G] free.
{end_of_verse}
